Subject: Materializes the slim call frame on demand

What this does
  Materializes the slim call frame on demand.

Why we need it
  A nested record frame's embedded `JSStackFrame` stored eight fields that duplicate fields of the record (`is_strict_mode`, `is_constructor`, `var_buf`, `arg_buf`, `arg_count`, `var_refs`, `var_ref_count`, `cur_gc_obj`) on every JS-to-JS call, though only cold paths (closure creation, the debugger, error paths, backtraces) read them; the hot return walk reads only `var_refs`/`var_ref_count`.

What it adds
  The fill stores only the hot fields; `regvm_sf_materialize(rt, sf)` reconstructs the dropped fields from the record on the cold readers (`is_strict_mode`, `js_get_stack_frame_at_level`, `get_var_ref`, `js_new_callsite_data`), recovering the record by frame-arena membership (`regvm_rec_of_sf`); compiled only under `QJS_REGVM_RECORD && !QJS_REGVM_INLOOP_CALL`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
--- a/quickjs.c
